<title>PORTUGAL: Portugal CPI fell 0.3 pct mo/mo in June.</title>
<headline>Portugal CPI fell 0.3 pct mo/mo in June.</headline>
<dateline>LISBON 1997-07-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Portuguese consumer prices (CPI) fell 0.3 percent month-on-month in June after rising 0.7 percent in May to give year-on-year inflation of 1.8 percent after 2.1 percent previously, the National Statistics Institute (INE) said.</p>
<p>The figure was better than analysts' forecasts which had ranged from a fall of 0.1 percent to a rise of 0.3 percent.</p>
<p>The rolling 12-month average stood at 2.9 percent, down from 3.0 percent in May.  </p>
<p> PORTUGUESE INFLATION	  June 97	 May 97    June 96</p>
<p> Monthly CPI rise		 -0.3	   +0.7	 -0.1</p>
<p> Yr-on-yr inflation	     +1.8	   +2.1	 +3.6</p>
<p> Average annual inflation     +2.9	   +3.0	 +3.3</p>
<p> Index (base 100 1991)	 133.8	  134.2	131.4</p>
<p> MAIN SECTORS		   JUNE 97	MAY 97	JUNE 96</p>
<p> Food and drink		 -0.9 pct    +1.1 pct     -0.4 pct</p>
<p> Shoes and clothing	   -0.2 pct    +0.1 pct     +0.1 pct</p>
<p> Health			   +0.4 pct    +0.2 pct     +0.1 pct</p>
<p> Transport			+0.1 pct    +0.3 pct     +0.2 pct</p>
<p> Education, entertainment    0.0 pct    +0.3 pct     +0.1 pct</p>
<p> Tobacco			  +1.5 pct    +2.4 pct     +1.6 pct</p>
<p>--Lisbon bureau 3511-3150035</p>
